Make the large-VIF1 barrier (patch 33) opt-in: GOW_VU1_EARLY_FINISH=1 enables it; it no longer follows
GOW_GS_FINISH_ASINCRONO. Patch 33 drained the worker and GS stage before every large VIF1 packet, the opposite of the
'early FINISH' planned in docs/research/handoff-2026-10-25-performance-phases.md (signal FINISH sooner, not wait).
GS stage push takes the queue lock once per packet: recycled buffers come from a per-producer pool refilled under it.
Static check that the VU1 history ring size is a power of two (patch 34 masks the index instead of using modulo).
Measured (Xeon E5-2666 v3 / RX 580, scale 2, scripted ship route, alternating A/B runs): 55.07/52.78 before,
54.71/52.36 after: no FPS change. Robustness/serialization fix only; no gain claimed.

